legitimately remain behind its fetched upstream. The CR acceptance runs inside
the same board/activity transaction callback as the `to-review` transition, so
a CR refusal rolls task and ancestor statuses back and publishes no activity.
A `task_delta` records no reviewed trunk OID at all — its base is a Story
branch tip, which is not a trunk commit and never becomes one. Accepted work never
stays in `reviewing`: a reviewer run that ends at bare `reviewing` with no
accepted Change Request is still cancelled and respawned, and the accepted branch
is derived from the record rather than from the status. `accept_cr` takes no
acknowledgement argument. `changes_requested` routes to `to-dev` or `analysis`
and the next producer publishes revision N+1 on the same branch and worktree;
prior revisions stay readable as immutable evidence. Stop-The-Line is unchanged.

A reviewer that is cancelled and respawned keeps its Change Request binding. The
successor inherits the revision, the CR id and the diff digest along with the
